Z||000000||jenniecartwright||10-10-2001||01:34 PM||||The part that goes over the roof and down the sides in the back of my 1987 Fiero has broke due to being side swiped.  I was told that all of the strength of the car was in this part.  Is it worth fixing?  Or is it true that all the strength is in that part? It is broken about half way up the drivers side, can it be replaced from there down by patching in a piece off another car or do I have to replace the entire thing if I can?  <BR>PLEASE E-MAIL ALL ANSWERS<BR>Thank you<BR>Jennie Cartwright||||reg||4
Z||000001||Tigger||10-10-2001||01:44 PM||||Very little if any stress goes through that, it's just the outer skin.  The real structure is the spaceframe behind it and if that looks to be intact then you should have no worries.<P>If you're planning on keeping the car for a long time, I'd look at finding a new rear clip just to avoid the worry of the repair failing and cracking the paint over a long time.  Lots more work but all depends what you want to do.<P>Whoops, was I supposed to email you?  Sorry    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Welcome to the forum!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-10-2001||03:44 PM||||If you want to come down to RI I have an entire notchback rear clip (roof section) from a red 85 GT you can have -ya just have to get it.||||reg||1
